{"version":3,"kind":"Notebook","sha256":"19bdfa7c46ab3e1a3f019388e950c6ab24329e32386faaa4519f53ec96104268","slug":"bmk-mode-converter","location":"/bmk_mode_converter.ipynb","dependencies":[],"frontmatter":{"title":"Mode converter benchmark","content_includes_title":false,"kernelspec":{"name":"python3","display_name":"Python 3","language":"python"},"github":"https://github.com/paulxshen/Luminescent.jl","numbering":{"title":{"offset":2}},"source_url":"https://github.com/paulxshen/Luminescent.jl/blob/main/docs/bmk_mode_converter.ipynb","edit_url":"https://github.com/paulxshen/Luminescent.jl/edit/main/docs/bmk_mode_converter.ipynb","exports":[{"format":"ipynb","filename":"bmk_mode_converter.ipynb","url":"/_public/bmk_mode_converter-416318d180320184a813e3465fd30468.ipynb"}]},"widgets":{},"mdast":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"block","kind":"notebook-content","children":[{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Benchmarks Luminescent against Tidy3D and Lumerical FDTD using the mode converter from Liu & Poon, ","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"key":"ZGAVBPvh9l"},{"type":"link","url":"https://arxiv.org/html/2506.16665v2","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"arXiv:2506.16665","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"key":"hlHvYmTXxG"}],"urlSource":"https://arxiv.org/html/2506.16665v2","key":"veXzhKutrh"},{"type":"text","value":", Sec. 3.4. The device is GDSFactory’s generic ","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"key":"ti8OLuA6h6"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"mode_converter(gap=0.15, length=20)","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"key":"LAweDrDHqe"},{"type":"text","value":": TE0 in a 500 nm waveguide couples to TE1 in a 1 µm waveguide over a 20 µm section, with 25 µm tapers to 1.2 µm. The narrow-arm S-bend is two 45° Euler bends as in the paper’s GDSFactory 7.8 version. Every port waveguide runs into the PML (the paper’s 10 µm extensions end inside the domain at the narrow ports). 220 nm Si, SiO2 cladding above and below. Si uses a lossless Lorentzian fit to the paper’s Palik model (n = 3.4729 at 1550 nm); SiO2 is constant n = 1.4425. The domain is the device plus 1 µm margins (the paper uses 72 × 10.5 × 4 µm³). TE0 enters the narrow input o2 with a λ/12 source bandwidth (the paper uses 20 nm). We report TE1 transmission and TE0 crosstalk at the wide output o3 (the paper’s cross port), sampled every 0.5 nm. The energy shutoff is 1e-5.","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"key":"a6tnOjfaDx"}],"key":"VukQnTi8m4"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":5,"column":1},"end":{"line":5,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Paper values (Tidy3D 2.7.7 on cloud GPUs, Lumerical 2025 R1 on a 24-core CPU; transmission and crosstalk digitized from Fig. 16):","position":{"start":{"line":5,"column":1},"end":{"line":5,"column":1}},"key":"HDc78TiFpY"}],"key":"jin0SRmyuf"},{"type":"table","position":{"start":{"line":7,"column":1},"end":{"line":13,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"tableRow","position":{"start":{"line":7,"column":1},"end":{"line":7,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"tableCell","header":true,"position":{"start":{"line":7,"column":1},"end":{"line":7,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"nres","position":{"start":{"line":7,"column":1},"end":{"line":7,"column":1}},"key":"YxxbxjVaLM"}],"key":"XJJWZ6heDv"},{"type":"tableCell","header":true,"position":{"start":{"line":7,"column":1},"end":{"line":7,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"TE1 Tidy3D / Lumerical","position":{"start":{"line":7,"column":1},"end":{"line":7,"column":1}},"key":"rqJy3yDn4Q"}],"key":"HWt8uCvkCh"},{"type":"tableCell","header":true,"position":{"start":{"line":7,"column":1},"end":{"line":7,"column":1}},"c